 "result": "**Mechanism:** a `ContextVar` plus werkzeug `LocalProxy` objects. All of it is in `src/tessel/globals.py`.\n\n- `_app_var` (line 40) is a `ContextVar[AppContext]` named `\"tessel.app_ctx\"`. It holds the current `AppContext`, which is set and reset when an app or request context is pushed or popped.\n- Each global is a `werkzeug.local.LocalProxy` bound to `_app_var`. It resolves the current context on every access and then reads one attribute from it:\n  - `active_app` (line 44) → `AppContext.app`, the `Tessel` instance.\n  - `g` (line 47) → `AppContext.g`, the `_AppCtxGlobals` object.\n  - `request` (line 57) → `AppContext.request`, a `Request`.\n  - `app_ctx` (line 41) is the `AppContext` itself. `session` (line 60) works the same way.\n\nThe proxies are `AppContext` (from `.ctx`), `Tessel` (`.app`), `_AppCtxGlobals` (`.ctx`) and `Request` (`.wrappers`). If no context is set, the proxy raises an error with `unbound_message`. `request` and `session` use the \"outside of request context\" message.\n\n`request_ctx` was merged into `app_ctx`, and the module-level `__getattr__` keeps a deprecated alias for it.",
